# Workshop open-source track rubric

Score for an open-source / community engineering workshop (0–100 total).
GitHub enrichment data may appear in the profile — use it for open_source only.

## Categories (required — use these exact keys)

### technical_skills (0–25)
Core languages and engineering fundamentals.

### open_source (0–35)
Contributions to others' repositories, GSoC-style programs, meaningful PRs — NOT merely owning personal repos.

### project_relevance (0–25)
Non-trivial projects with documentation or adoption signals.

### prior_experience (0–15)
Production or internship experience shipping code.

## Fairness
Do NOT score based on institution, GPA, gender, or location.

## Threshold guidance
- final_score ≥ 65 → APPROVE
- 45–64 → WAITLIST or MANUAL_REVIEW
- below 45 → REJECT

